<title>USA: OMI-run ship leaks fuel in San Francisco.</title>
<headline>OMI-run ship leaks fuel in San Francisco.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>OMI Corp said Friday that a U.S. government cargo vessel operated by OMI Ship Management Inc has leaked about 8,400 gallons of fuel oil into San Francisco Bay.</p>
<p>OMI said vessel Cape Mohican was discovered to be leaking fuel oil on October 28, while the vessel was in drydock and under the control of a local shipyard in San Francisco.</p>
<p>The company said that the U.S. Coast Guard and the shipyard assumed control of the clean-up, and OMI provided assistance.</p>
